From cc74980c346ebede53b926576d533580e72e488e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: wizard keeps Samba off and describes the logins
 correctly

The first-run wizard turned Samba on when it showed its page ("# Enable
samba"), so Hades' default of Samba off (password protected when enabled)
was lost for everyone who just clicked through. Keep Samba's real state;
the switch on the same page still enables it, with a generated password.

Its texts also said that SSH logs in with root and the default password,
which Hades' sshd refuses. New texts for SSH (key, or a password set first)
and Samba (off by default; generated password shown in its settings).
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po |  8 ++++++++
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po |  8 ++++++++
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po |  8 ++++++++
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po |  8 ++++++++
 resources/lib/modules/services.py                     | 10 ++++------
 5 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index c6b54ed..61aa1b8 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1151,3 +1151,11 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#32916"
 msgid "Set to ON to enable the embedded SSH server. Log in as 'root' with an SSH key, or set a password first: while root has the default password, password logins are refused."
 msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32917"
+msgid "@DISTRONAME@ also supports SSH for remote access. This is for advanced users who wish to interact with @DISTRONAME@'s underlying operating system. Log in as [COLOR blue]root[/COLOR] with an SSH key, or set a password first: while root has the default password, password logins are refused."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32918"
+msgid "@DISTRONAME@ includes a Samba server to share files with your computers through Finder or Windows Explorer. It is off by default. When you turn it on, a password is generated for it; you can look it up and change it in the Samba settings."
+msgstr ""
